From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter Laux <hunterlaux@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 22:30:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 29/29] mips: jz47xx: x2600: SPL: eMMC data at the middle of
 the sample window

The SPL reads the eMMC at 25 MHz with the sample point the boot ROM
leaves in MSC0CDR, RX phase 0. On an X2600E unit with an A31M8C eMMC
every data read then fails with a data CRC error, while commands and
reads at 400 kHz work. Swept on that unit, reads are correct from RX
phase 1 to 5 (2 to 5 with the TX phase at 270 degrees).

Set RX phase 3 with tuning off when switching to the data clock, as
Ingenic's soc_mmc_set_rx_phase() does for its working clock.

Signed-off-by: Hunter Laux <hunterlaux@gmail.com>
---
 arch/mips/mach-jz47xx/x2600/spl_emmc.c | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/mips/mach-jz47xx/x2600/spl_emmc.c b/arch/mips/mach-jz47xx/x2600/spl_emmc.c
index 98ed2353..682a1166 100644
--- a/arch/mips/mach-jz47xx/x2600/spl_emmc.c
+++ b/arch/mips/mach-jz47xx/x2600/spl_emmc.c
@@ -73,6 +73,10 @@
 #define CDR_BUSY		BIT(28)
 #define CDR_STOP		BIT(27)
 #define CDR_EXCK_E		BIT(21)	/* SDK MSCCDR_EXCK_E, in MSC0CDR */
+#define CDR_TUNING_OFF		BIT(20)	/* set: the fixed phases below */
+#define CDR_RX_PHASE_SHIFT	17	/* 19:17, the sample point */
+#define CDR_RX_PHASE_MASK	(7 << CDR_RX_PHASE_SHIFT)
+#define CDR_RX_PHASE_DATA	3
 #define CDR_DIV_MASK		0xff
 /* what the boot ROM's cpm_desc leaves (ad5x_spl_image.py): APLL / 16 */
 #define MSC0CDR_BOOT_ROM	0x20108003
@@ -141,6 +145,17 @@ static void emmc_set_clock(bool fast)
 		setbits_le32(CPM_MSC0CDR, CDR_EXCK_E);
 	val = readl(CPM_MSC0CDR) & ~(3U << CDR_PARENT_SHIFT);
 	val |= parent << CDR_PARENT_SHIFT;
+	/*
+	 * The sample point for the 25 MHz data clock, tuning off (Ingenic's
+	 * soc_mmc_set_rx_phase()). What the boot ROM leaves, 0, fails with
+	 * data CRC errors on an X2600E unit's eMMC (A31M8C), which reads
+	 * correctly from 1 (2 with the TX phase at 270 degrees) to 5: 3, the
+	 * middle. Identification at 400 kHz keeps the boot ROM's.
+	 */
+	if (fast) {
+		val &= ~CDR_RX_PHASE_MASK;
+		val |= CDR_TUNING_OFF | CDR_RX_PHASE_DATA << CDR_RX_PHASE_SHIFT;
+	}
 	val &= ~(CDR_STOP | CDR_BUSY | CDR_DIV_MASK);
 	writel(val | CDR_CE | div, CPM_MSC0CDR);
 	for (val = 0; (readl(CPM_MSC0CDR) & CDR_BUSY) && val < 10000; val++)
-- 
